  "corpus_url": "https://github.com/golang/crypto.git",
  "corpus_pinned_commit": "7a4a4d6beae2222add4437a0910bd48414e19211",
  "scanned_files": [
   "ssh/cipher.go",
   "ssh/mac.go",
   "ssh/mlkem.go"
  ],
  "annotation_method": "INDEPENDENT TOKEN SWEEP, then hand adjudication of every hit. The sweep token list was written from the Go standard library package names, the SSH wire-identifier sets in RFC 4253/5656/8731, and NIST SP 800-131A -- NOT from engine/scanner.py. A sweep derived from the tool's own rules would label every finding positive and make every miss invisible. Each swept line was then read and judged against the criterion in benchmark/labels/README.md; the residue is negative by exhaustion."
 },
 "annotation": {
  "annotated_by": "IndraMesh benchmark harness author, by direct reading of every line in scope",
  "unit": "one (file, 1-based line) location",
  "files_in_scope": 3,
  "candidate_lines_swept": 94,
  "positive_labels_L1": 47,
  "positive_labels_L2_only": 2,
  "negative_labels_audited": 23,
  "method": "A location is POSITIVE in L1 iff it names, or binds a name to, a quantum-vulnerable cryptographic primitive in a position that determines the algorithm: P1 factory call or mode registration, P1b naming a primitive identifier in executable code, P2 a key-spec/hash binding, P3 an import that determines the algorithm downstream, P4 an SSH/OpenSSL algorithm identifier. A line that merely OPERATES on a primitive chosen elsewhere is NEGATIVE in L1 and POSITIVE in L2; the harness reports both.",
  "deliberate_exclusions": "ML-KEM is labelled NEGATIVE, and this is the most consequential judgement in the set. crypto/mlkem is FIPS 203 -- post-quantum, the REMEDY. The criterion asks for quantum-VULNERABLE primitives, so labelling ML-KEM a vulnerability would invert the meaning of the scan. Poly1305 is negative for the narrower reason that it is in neither declared break model in pqtaxonomy.py.",
  "scope_caveat": "THREE files, not the package. The other 28 non-test files under ssh/ were swept but NOT annotated and are NOT scanned. Recall here is relative to these three files only and says nothing about the rest of x/crypto. This is a small corpus: denominators are printed beside every ratio, and the figure should be read as a smoke test of the Go pack, not as a characterisation of Go detection.",
  "label_corrections": "Corrected after the first measurement, in the direction AGAINST the tool: one missed RC4 positive added (which lowers measured precision), two chacha20 read-path positives added (which removes two false positives), and two L1/L2 rows corrected so the L2 variant is not silently identical to L1. The original token sweep was case-sensitive and missed lowercase qualified calls such as `rc4.NewCipher`; the first annotation pass also labelled only one of two structurally identical call sites. A detector that scores well against incomplete labels is not evidence of anything, which is the reason these were found and fixed rather than tuned around."
 },
